# Functional Programming
# Functional programming is a programming paradigm that treats computation as the evaluation of mathematical functions and avoids changing state and mutable data.
# It emphasizes the use of pure functions, higher-order functions, and immutability. In functional programming, functions are first-class citizens, meaning they can be passed as arguments, returned from other functions, and assigned to variables.
